WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.020
Decision tools help teams make reasoning visible.

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.620
A decision matrix compares options against criteria.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.095
Weighted criteria show which factors matter more.

00:00:08.095 --> 00:00:12.380
A decision tree maps choices, uncertain events, and possible consequences at a high level.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:17.280
A risk register captures risks, likelihood, impact, owners, mitigations, and status.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.445
These tools are useful when they support judgment rather than replace it.

00:00:20.445 --> 00:00:24.315
Cost-benefit thinking helps teams compare what an option requires against what it is

00:00:24.315 --> 00:00:25.300
expected to produce.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.660
The cost is not only money.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.140
It can include time, attention, operational burden, technical debt, training, disruption,

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.580
and loss of optionality.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.460
Benefits can include safety, reliability, revenue, learning, trust, resilience,

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:37.280
or reduced risk.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.435
Good analysis makes both sides visible.

00:00:39.435 --> 00:00:43.190
Decision records are especially valuable in technical and operational environments.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.975
A good record captures the frame, decision owner, options considered, criteria, evidence,

00:00:47.975 --> 00:00:50.790
assumptions, tradeoffs, risks, and the reason for the chosen path.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.720
It also records what would cause the decision to be revisited.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.435
This makes decisions reviewable instead of mysterious.

00:00:56.435 --> 00:00:58.255
Team decisions need role clarity.

00:00:58.255 --> 00:01:01.620
People should know who is giving input, who is advising, who is deciding,

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.780
who is executing, and who must be informed.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.380
Disagreement should be welcomed when it improves the decision,

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.350
but it also needs a path to closure.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.980
Psychological safety, in practical terms, means people can raise concerns,

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:15.620
share uncertainty, and challenge assumptions without being punished for useful candor.

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.460
After-action reviews close the loop.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.300
They compare expected results with actual outcomes, examine what was known at the time,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.740
and identify what should change in future decisions.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.455
The best teams do not use tools to perform certainty.

00:01:26.455 --> 00:01:30.480
They use tools to clarify judgment, create accountability, and learn over time.
